  "provenance": [
    {
      "source_type": "manufacturer-pdf",
      "source": "Topps official checklist PDF: 2023ToppsSeries1BaseballChecklistV2.pdf",
      "retrieved": "2026-08-07",
      "covers": "Series 1 (#1-330) and its inserts",
      "notes": "Four relic programmes run in both series under one name while reusing their card codes for different players, so they are kept per series rather than merged: 1988 Topps Baseball Relics, Cut Signatures, In The Name Relics and Major League Material Cards. 88R-AB is Adrian Beltre in Series 1 and Alex Bregman in Series 2, ITN-AB is Andrew Benintendi and then Alex Bregman, and there are 23 such collisions across the four. Merging would have silently dropped one player of each pair. Topps prints \"22GHA-AP Albert Pujols St. Louis Cardinals\" twice in the 2022 Greatest Hits Autographs section, seven lines apart and identical on every field, so the section holds 15 cards and not the 16 lines it lists. The repeat is dropped and the converter now drops any line repeated identically inside one section. Where Topps reuses a code for genuinely different players — 88BA-AR is both Adley Rutschman and Austin Riley, 88BA-MMA both Miles Mastrobuoni and Manny Machado, 88BA-RD both Reid Detmers and Rafael Devers, PPA-AR the Rutschman/Riley pair again — both rows are kept, because those are two cards."
    },
    {
      "source_type": "manufacturer-pdf",
      "source": "Topps official checklist PDF: MLB2302-2023ToppsSeries2BBChecklistFinalv2.pdf",
      "retrieved": "2026-08-07",
      "covers": "Series 2 (#331-660) and its inserts",
      "notes": "This document prints its relic marker as RELICS and places these four programmes after the AUTOGRAPH marker, so they arrived as autographs and were refiled as relics to match Series 1. Topps also heads eleven sections AUTOGRAPH PARALLEL or AUTOGRAPH VARIATION, and neither is a parallel here. Nine reuse their parent checklist's card numbers exactly and are recorded as autograph checklists declaring varies, an autograph of a card sharing that card's number. The two oversized ones number themselves independently — 88LLA-AJ against the parent's 88LL-1 — so they introduce cards, which a variation must never do, and they are autograph checklists with no varies. Both readings follow the rule in ROW-FORMAT: a signature is not a colour, and an autographed subset is not a partial parallel."
    }
  ]
